00:13:50,143 --> 00:13:51,451
What is this?

243
00:13:51,475 --> 00:13:53,635
I was rubbish at numbers at school.

244
00:13:53,646 --> 00:13:56,148
Well, all the best people were
rubbish at numbers at school.

245
00:13:56,150 --> 00:13:57,416
But I don't know anything.

246
00:13:57,418 --> 00:14:00,685
You talk about my working
at Mr. Mason's farm, but how?

247
00:14:00,687 --> 00:14:03,155
I couldn't balance the books
if my life depended on it.

248
00:14:03,157 --> 00:14:04,695
Why do you need to?

249
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:07,748
Because I want to be grown-up,
Mrs. Patmore.

250
00:14:07,767 --> 00:14:10,195
I want responsibility.
I want to be an adult.

251
00:14:10,197 --> 00:14:13,698
I can't just stand here following
orders for the rest of my life.

252
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:16,268
What education and knowledge

253
00:14:16,402 --> 00:14:19,838
does for all these people
is to give them choices.

254
00:14:19,972 --> 00:14:23,975
And choices weren't something
that people had before.

255
00:14:24,110 --> 00:14:28,817
And that I think is what's the sort of
running theme through series five.

256
00:14:28,828 --> 00:14:31,450
There are suddenly
more choices for people.

257
00:14:31,452 --> 00:14:34,319
And series five definitely
has even greater revelations

258
00:14:34,454 --> 00:14:39,324
for people in relation to the
possibilities outside of Downton

259
00:14:39,459 --> 00:14:41,073
and within Downton as well.

260
00:14:41,074 --> 00:14:43,495
Thomas comes to mind as
one of the biggest ones.

261
00:14:43,497 --> 00:14:47,232
He really takes his own life in
hand and tries to... tries to

262
00:14:47,234 --> 00:14:49,216
make changes in his own life,

263
00:14:49,239 --> 00:14:52,034
and I think it's one of the most
compelling stories we have this year.

264
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:54,690
It's a fantastic story
because you sort of

265
00:14:54,713 --> 00:14:57,676
scratch the surface
of Thomas more,

266
00:14:57,678 --> 00:15:02,648
and you realize that he's a person
that just wants to find love

267
00:15:02,671 --> 00:15:06,952
and find somebody
that accepts him for who he is.

268
00:15:06,954 --> 00:15:10,889
If anyone had told me that
I'd have been friends with a...

269
00:15:11,023 --> 00:15:15,060
A man like you,
I'd have not have believed them.

270
00:15:15,194 --> 00:15:17,149
But we have been friends.

271
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:20,120
I hope you find some happiness.

272
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,997
I do, truly.

273
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:26,856
I think that what we're
finding in season five is the world

274
00:15:26,857 --> 00:15:29,424
is changing and people are...

275
00:15:29,448 --> 00:15:32,008
The younger generation,
certainly, is saying,

276
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:35,714
"no, we're not going to marry
someone who's just suitable."

277
00:15:35,716 --> 00:15:39,417
And that's the running story
through the romance

278
00:15:39,419 --> 00:15:43,636
and the intrigue
and the scandal in this is...

279
00:15:43,660 --> 00:15:46,489
It's young people saying,
"I'll marry for love

280
00:15:46,513 --> 00:15:53,031
and not because he's got all the right...
He ticks all the right boxes for family."

281
00:15:53,033 --> 00:15:54,699
The war
and the changes that followed

282
00:15:54,701 --> 00:15:57,702
have created a younger,
freer generation.

283
00:15:57,704 --> 00:16:00,944
People want to be happy
and live the life they want,

284
00:16:00,956 --> 00:16:03,808
not necessarily the one that has
been laid out for them.

285
00:16:03,810 --> 00:16:08,213
Even Lady Mary and Lord Gillingham
are taking hold of these new ideas.

286
00:16:08,215 --> 00:16:12,809
Here's a season five clip
that's quite saucy.

