quite capable of blowing

702
00:39:55,507 --> 00:39:57,240
a marriage out of the water.

703
00:39:57,242 --> 00:40:00,136
And that was a sort of
ripple of danger

704
00:40:00,147 --> 00:40:02,746
they all lived with
and of course indulged.

705
00:40:02,748 --> 00:40:05,515
You know, there is something
about human beings that they

706
00:40:05,517 --> 00:40:09,570
like to take risks, and I think we,
you know, in <i>Downton</i>,

707
00:40:09,571 --> 00:40:13,624
we just sort of plug into that.

708
00:40:13,626 --> 00:40:17,694
You know, my mother's always
telling me never put anything in writing.

709
00:40:17,696 --> 00:40:20,731
And now thanks to you,
I never will again.

710
00:40:20,733 --> 00:40:23,266
The first four seasons of
<i>Downton Abbey</i> takes place

711
00:40:23,282 --> 00:40:26,006
between 1912 and 1923,

712
00:40:26,018 --> 00:40:29,496
and writer Julian Fellowes
and the whole production team

713
00:40:29,519 --> 00:40:33,300
have taken great pains
to get every period detail correct,

714
00:40:33,323 --> 00:40:36,546
including some
cultural biases that today

715
00:40:36,548 --> 00:40:40,584
may seem politically incorrect
or even abhorrent,

716
00:40:40,586 --> 00:40:43,587
such as the scandal of homosexuality.

717
00:40:43,589 --> 00:40:47,157
Remember this scene when Thomas,
the man with a secret,

718
00:40:47,159 --> 00:40:51,762
misunderstands his fellow
servant Jimmy's kindness?

719
00:40:51,764 --> 00:40:54,197
What are you doing?!
Why are you in here?!

720
00:40:54,199 --> 00:40:56,137
Because of all there is between us.

721
00:40:56,161 --> 00:40:59,460
There's nothing between us
except my fist if you don't get out!

722
00:41:00,186 --> 00:41:02,305
We see some quite realistic

723
00:41:02,307 --> 00:41:05,776
and horrible attitudes towards Thomas,
you know?

724
00:41:05,778 --> 00:41:07,878
Homophobic attitudes,
because that's what it was like then.

725
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:11,381
To finally discuss that and see that
and see Thomas completely destroyed

726
00:41:11,516 --> 00:41:14,585
and just at the end of it
a vulnerable human being

727
00:41:14,586 --> 00:41:17,654
who just needs affection
and has never been given it.

728
00:41:17,656 --> 00:41:23,226
I cannot hide that I find
your situation revolting,

729
00:41:23,228 --> 00:41:28,298
but whether or not you believe me,
I am not entirely unsympathetic.

730
00:41:28,300 --> 00:41:32,335
You have been twisted
by nature into something foul,

731
00:41:32,358 --> 00:41:35,605
and even I can see
that you did not ask for it.

732
00:41:42,250 --> 00:41:45,550
I'm not foul, Mr. Carson.

733
00:41:45,573 --> 00:41:48,752
I'm not the same as you,
but I am not foul.

734
00:41:48,754 --> 00:41:51,988
Carson would dearly love to
get rid of Thomas,

735
00:41:52,123 --> 00:41:55,225
but when getting rid of Thomas
means that there will be a family scandal

736
00:41:55,226 --> 00:41:58,328
and the scandal would reflect
badly on the house,

737
00:41:58,330 --> 00:42:01,732
then the pragmatic side of Carson
comes out, and he thinks,

738
00:42:01,734 --> 00:42:05,235
right, well I'll suppress my personal
feelings for this loathsome person

739
00:42:05,237 --> 00:42:10,974
and for the good of the house,
I will swallow my pride and accept him.

740
00:42:10,976 --> 00:42:15,278
Carson's reluctant acceptance
of Thomas's homosexuality

741
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:18,715
mirrors the feelings of society
at large in this period.

742
00:42:18,717 --> 00:42:21,084
Perhaps this has twisted Thomas

743
00:42:21,086 --> 00:42:25,400
into the nefarious character
we love to hate.

744
00:42:25,412 --> 00:42:29,545
Here, Thomas blackmails Baxter,
Lady Cora's maid,

745
00:42:29,568 --> 00:42:32,431
to spy on members
of the Crawley family.

746
00:42:32,454 --> 00:42:34,998
What deep secret does he hold
over her?

747
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:37,456
You've got to find out more.

748
00:42:39,311 --> 00:42:41,742
- But how?
- You'll think of something.

749
00:42:41,765 --> 00:42:44,040
Thomas and Baxter have history.

750
00:42:44,042 --> 00:42:46,738
He has a dark secret
that he knows about her,

751
00:42:46,762 --> 00:42:48,245
so he has a hold over her.

752
00:42:48,247 --> 00:42:53,150
Basically, the situation that
she has found herself in

753
00:42:53,284 --> 00:42:56,620
is one that would mean she would not
be able to work in those times.

754
00:42:56,754 --> 00:43:00,795
She would probably have to
live in a poor house

755
00:43:00,819 --> 00:43:07,748
and maybe work as a prostitute
if she wanted to get any food, really.

756
00:43:07,749 --> 00:43:11,835
So Thomas gets somebody
who's very down on their luck

757
00:43:11,837 --> 00:43:15,238
and goes, "I can help,
but you'll have to help me back."

758
00:43:15,240 --> 00:43:18,932
So that's the carrot that he dangles,
and then the stick is very much,

759
00:43:18,956 --> 00:43:20,599
"you don't get something for nothing, love.

760
00:43:20,623 --> 00:43:23,451
"You're gonna be my eyes and ears
on the ground upstairs,

761
00:43:23,474 --> 00:43:26,850
and you're going to tell me everything
that goes on, and I can use this."

762
00:43:26,852 --> 00:43:30,435
So he's very much got himself
an upstairs spy.

763
00:43:30,459 --> 00:43:32,196
Now listen...

764
00:43:32,784 --> 00:43:38,072
What you have to decide is
where your first loyalties are.

765
00:43:38,095 --> 00:43:40,925
With her... Or with me?

766
00:43:41,183 --> 00:43:43,400
All right.

767
00:43:43,402 --> 00:43:47,504
- Have it your own way.
- Oh, I intend to.

768
00:43:47,506 --> 00:43:53,677
Baxter does find a friend in Moseley,
formerly valet to Matthew Crawley

769
00:43:53,679 --> 00:43:56,780
and currently a footman at Downton
and one of my favorite characters.

770
00:43:56,782 --> 00:44:00,016
I think they have a shared
kinship between them.

771
00:44:00,018 --> 00:44:02,586
Certainly, they have both seen
their share of misfortune.

772
00:44:02,588 --> 00:44:05,889
I think he feels with Baxter
that there have been injustices

773
00:44:06,023 --> 00:44:12,028
in her life, and...
And so I think he responds to that.

774
00:44:12,163 --> 00:44:16,350
And he knows that
Thomas has a history of

775
00:44:16,351 --> 00:44:20,537
manipulating circumstance
and manipulating people.

776
00:44:20,539 --> 00:44:24,641
And so he feels that Baxter is
at the rough end of that

777
00:44:24,643 --> 00:44:27,344
and wants to put a sort of
a comforting arm around her.

778
00:44:27,346 --> 00:44:30,094
Leave her alone, Mr. Barrow.

779
00:44:30,117 --> 00:44:31,761
We don't want any bullying

780
00:44:31,784 --> 00:44:34,551
brought back from overseas,
do we, Ms. Baxter?

781
00:44:34,553 --> 00:44:37,988
Now are there any stalls
you'd still like to see?

782
00:44:46,764 --> 00:44:51,257
Thomas doesn't take kindly to
Moseley's interference in season five,

783
00:44:51,280 --> 00:44:55,410
and his patience grows thin
with Baxter withholding valuable information

784
00:44:55,434 --> 00:45:00,143
which he could use to spread his misery
and better his position in the house.

785
00:45:00,145 --> 00:45:03,446
Will Thomas reveal Baxter's
dark secret?

786
00:45:03,448 --> 00:45:06,449
Will that crush the budding
affections of Baxter and Mosley

787
00:45:06,451 --> 00:45:08,318
and send her away from Downton?

788
00:45:08,320 --> 00:45:11,321
Take a look at this season five clip.

789
00:45:12,037 --> 00:45:15,911
There's no point trying to
find Mr. Mosley...

790
00:45:17,395 --> 00:45:20,095
Because he can't help you now.

791
00:45:23,916 --> 00:45:26,370
If that's how you want to play it,

792
00:45:26,394 --> 00:45:28,571
I'll give you until
upstairs dinner has finished.

793
00:45:28,573 --> 00:45:31,278
After which,
I will ask to speak to her Ladyship,

794
00:45:31,302 --> 00:45:33,944
and I will tell her your story.

795
00:45:33,967 --> 00:45:36,327
Do you hear what I'm saying?

796
00:45:37,736 --> 00:45:42,786
- I can't tell you what I don't know.
- But you know something.

797
00:45:42,788 --> 00:45:46,089
And I think it links Mr. Bates
to the dead valet.

798
00:45:53,397 --> 00:45:56,580
Um, I just don't
like that Thomas Barrow.

799
00:45:56,581 --> 00:46:00,804
Season five will reveal Baxter's secret,
and it's a doozy.

800
00:46:00,806 --> 00:46:03,006
I just can't wait.

801
00:46:03,008 --> 00:46:05,926
In season four,
we met many new characters,

802
00:46:05,937 --> 00:46:10,080
and one in particular was scandalous
just to lay eyes on.

803
00:46:10,082 --> 00:46:13,984
Is anyone there?

804
00:46:13,986 --> 00:46:15,919
I think this is where we're
supposed to be.

805
00:46:15,921 --> 00:46:19,823
When he actually arrives at Downton,
this is a complete shock.

806
00:46:19,957 --> 00:46:25,434
The below stairs staff have perhaps
almost never seen a black man.

807
00:46:25,458 --> 00:46:28,675
I particularly enjoyed
the scene below stairs

808
00:46:28,685 --> 00:46:31,926
when he arrives and Carson,
as soon as he claps eyes on Jack,

809
00:46:31,949 --> 00:46:35,472
you know,
he's completely shocked.

810
00:46:35,474 --> 00:46:38,184
Welcome to Downton.

811
00:46:40,379 --> 00:46:44,514
And this then follows, of course,
this extremely awkward conversation.

812
00:46:44,516 --> 00:46:47,784
Have you never thought of
visiting Africa?

813
00:46:47,786 --> 00:46:50,186
And why should I go to Africa,
Mr. Carson?

814
00:46:50,188 --> 00:46:52,655
I'm no more African than you are.

815
00:46:52,657 --> 00:46:54,958
It's really interesting to
see all the different

816
00:46:54,960 --> 00:46:59,229
characters' attitudes towards race,
and certainly,

817
00:46:59,231 --> 00:47:03,233
some of the characters are more
forward-thinking and open-minded than others.

818
00:47:03,235 --> 00:47:06,102
Certainly, Cousin Rose
is a character who is always

819
00:47:06,104 --> 00:47:08,972
forward-thinking,
perhaps more so than any other.

820
00:47:08,974 --> 00:47:12,909
To Rose, Jack Ross was not only
a talented singer

821
00:47:12,911 --> 00:47:17,647
but an enticing eligible bachelor.
Remember, this was the 1920s.

822
00:47:17,649 --> 00:47:20,963
Interracial relationships were
a rare thing,

823
00:47:20,986 --> 00:47:24,720
but cousin Rose is always
breaking down barriers, isn't she,

824
00:47:24,744 --> 00:47:27,457
and seizing the moment?

825
00:47:27,459 --> 00:47:30,126
Don't... Don't do that.

826
00:47:30,150 --> 00:47:32,686
Rose is immature, and she's rash.

827
00:47:32,709 --> 00:47:34,259
She follows her heart.

828
00:47:34,283 --> 00:47:36,886
She doesn't think too carefully
about things,

829
00:47:36,909 --> 00:47:40,799
and I think that any suggestion of
a relationship there

830
00:47:40,823 --> 00:47:45,151
is completely out of the question
and would be disastrous for Rose.

831
00:47:45,175 --> 00:47:47,206
Rose, I like you very much.
I want you to know.

832
00:47:47,218 --> 00:47:48,263
But?

833
00:47:48,286 --> 00:47:51,114
Well, what can we hope
to come out of all this?

834
00:47:51,116 --> 00:47:53,817
Can't we just be in the moment?

835
00:47:53,819 --> 00:47:55,251
I don't know many men like you,

836
00:47:55,253 --> 00:47:57,654
and you don't know
many girls like me.

837
00:47:57,656 --> 00:48:01,624
- Ain't that the truth?
- Then let's enjoy it.

838
00:48:01,626 --> 00:48:04,994
You know what the French say...
<i>vive la difference</i>

839
00:48:05,664 --> 00:48:11,101
I didn't want Jack to turn
into someone we feel sorry for.

840
00:48:11,103 --> 00:48:13,002
I mean,
he's a very successful man.

841
00:48:13,004 --> 00:48:14,204
He's a successful singer.

842
00:48:14,206 --> 00:48:17,699
He's got a good career,
but nevertheless,

843
00:48:17,722 --> 00:48:21,478
society at that time
was comparatively racist

844
00:48:21,480 --> 00:48:26,382
in that even people
who were perfectly normal

845
00:48:26,384 --> 00:48:30,420
would still have difficulty
accepting that union.

846
00:48:30,422 --> 00:48:32,589
And certainly,
the color issue is a non-starter.

847
00:48:32,591 --> 00:48:36,771
Jack knows that, really,
and it doesn't take terribly much to persuade him.

848
00:48:36,794 --> 00:48:38,380
Tell me honestly,

849
00:48:38,403 --> 00:48:41,949
do you think you can survive
what they'll do to you?

850
00:48:41,972 --> 00:48:43,733
Because
I don't believe Rose could.

851
00:48:43,735 --> 00:48:47,495
It may come as something of
a relief for you to hear that

852
00:48:47,615 --> 00:48:49,917
I will not be marrying Rose.

853
00:48:49,940 --> 00:48:51,831
You won't?

854
00:48:51,854 --> 00:48:52,993
No.

855
00:48:53,017 --> 00:48:55,345
I don't want to spoil her life.

856
00:48:55,347 --> 00:48:58,748
Alas, Rose and Jack
were not meant to be.

857
00:48:58,750 --> 00:49:01,651
What will season five hold
for our rebellious Rose?

858
00:49:01,653 --> 00:49:04,821
Are there new taboo dalliances
coming up?

859
00:49:04,823 --> 00:49:07,724
I'll be keeping an eye on her.

860
00:49:08,307 --> 00:49:10,627
Certainly Rose is not the only
one to indulge in some

861
00:49:10,629 --> 00:49:12,761
scandalous love affairs.

862
00:49:14,332 --> 00:49:17,600
My dear, this is...
Isn't what it seems.

863
00:49:17,602 --> 00:49:19,903
Is there room for misinterpretation?

864
00:49:19,905 --> 00:49:22,539
Remember when Robert
was caught kissing a maid

865
00:49:22,541 --> 00:49:25,775
or Lady Edith kissing the farmer
and later falling in love with

866
00:49:25,777 --> 00:49:28,611
a married man
and having his love child?

867
00:49:28,613 --> 00:49:33,016
I suspect there will be much
more about this in season five.

868
00:49:33,018 --> 00:49:37,487
Since Matthew's unexpected death
at the end of season three,

869
00:49:37,489 --> 00:49:40,456
we've all been wondering if
Lady Mary will ever love again.

870
00:49:40,458 --> 00:49:44,494
Well, season four certainly gave
us two suitable candidates,

871
00:49:44,496 --> 00:49:47,163
Charles Blake and Tony Gillingham.

872
00:49:47,165 --> 00:49:51,201
By the end of the season,
Mary seems torn between the two.

873
00:49:51,203 --> 00:49:54,856
But as we saw
earlier in our program,

874
00:49:54,880 --> 00:49:58,708
Lord Gillingham proposed that
he and Mary get to know each other

875
00:49:58,731 --> 00:50:02,845
while away for a weekend
to see how they get on.

876
00:50:02,869 --> 00:50:05,415
Let's see what Lady Mary decided.

877
00:50:12,724 --> 00:50:15,096
It's mad not to give
a false name.

878
00:50:15,119 --> 00:50:17,460
Always make a lie
as truthful as possible.

879
00:50:17,462 --> 00:50:19,696
How did you manage to
get the rooms connected?

880
00:50:19,698 --> 00:50:22,632
Well, I'm not a complete half-wit.

881
00:50:22,634 --> 00:50:26,336
Nor, happily, is the manager.

882
00:50:26,749 --> 00:50:30,084
So, what's the plan?

883
00:50:30,096 --> 00:50:31,610
It's a simple one.

884
00:50:31,634 --> 00:50:35,015
We'll go down to Church Street
for a scrumptious dinner,

885
00:50:35,036 --> 00:50:38,171
after which...
We'll come back.

886
00:50:38,195 --> 00:50:41,417
- And make love.
- Exactly.

887
00:50:42,248 --> 00:50:45,241
We'll make love all night,
and in fact,

888
00:50:45,265 --> 00:50:48,419
for as long as either of us
has any stamina left.

889
00:50:48,431 --> 00:50:51,034
And who can say fairer than that?

890
00:50:51,057 --> 00:50:55,064
Oh, my, my, does this mean that
Mary will marry Tony, Lord Gillingham?

891
00:50:55,066 --> 00:50:57,767
What will happen
if the family finds out?

892
00:50:57,769 --> 00:51:01,571
I know there is a wedding
in season five, but is it Mary's?

893
00:51:01,573 --> 00:51:06,309
That's why Julian Fellowes
always keeps us guessing.

894
00:51:06,311 --> 00:51:09,145
Stay with us after
this brief intermission,

895
00:51:09,147 --> 00:51:11,309
and we'll have another scene
from season five

896
00:51:11,332 --> 00:51:15,985
that might give us a clue to
who's getting married in our upcoming season.

897
00:51:15,987 --> 00:51:18,087
You won't want to miss it.

898
00:51:24,695 --> 00:51:27,463
Thank you for joining me,
Bernadette Peters,

899
00:51:27,598 --> 00:51:30,333
for this loving look back
at all things <i>Downton Abbey</i>.

900
00:51:30,467 --> 00:51:33,691
It's been so much fun.
As we've mentioned,

901
00:51:33,714 --> 00:51:38,007
here's an exclusive look at
a few more moments from season five.

902
00:51:38,009 --> 00:51:40,576
- Isn't it absurd?
- I don't know,

903
00:51:40,599 --> 00:51:44,380
might be rather fun for her to reinvent herself
as a great lady of the county.

904
00:51:44,515 --> 00:51:46,716
For the last time, are you certain
you know what you're doing?

905
00:51:46,718 --> 00:51:48,496
I believe so.

906
00:51:48,519 --> 00:51:51,067
Fashionably late is one thing.

907
00:51:51,091 --> 00:51:54,857
I'm fairly sure this was our
very biggest day in the history

908
00:51:54,859 --> 00:51:58,361
of <i>Downton Abbey</i> in the sense
that literally everybody in the town,

909
00:51:58,363 --> 00:52:00,697
everybody upstairs,
everybody downstairs is all

910
00:52:00,699 --> 00:52:02,265
gathered for this big moment.

911
00:52:02,267 --> 00:52:05,766
Need your help. If you see anyone
that shouldn't be filming,

912
00:52:05,785 --> 00:52:08,309
if you see anyone with a phone,
with a camera they shouldn't have,

913
00:52:08,332 --> 00:52:10,640
please report it
to an A.D. straightaway.

914
00:52:10,642 --> 00:52:13,443
We want to keep this special for
the British public,

915
00:52:13,459 --> 00:52:15,139
and that means not having a photo

916
00:52:15,162 --> 00:52:18,150
of our bride on the front page
of a paper tomorrow.

917
